source: crates/ruff_python_formatter/tests/fixtures.rs
input_file: crates/ruff_python_formatter/resources/test/fixtures/ruff/identity_operators.by
---
## Input
```bython
# basedpython spells identity as `===` / `!==`. both parse to the `CmpOp` of
# `is` / `is not`, whose surface form is instead a parametric type test, so the
# two spellings must not be collapsed into one

xs = [1]

a = xs === xs
b = xs !== xs

# the `is` spelling is a type test and stays as written
c = xs is list[int]
d = xs is not list[int]

# a chain of identity comparisons is ordinary python, and each operator keeps
# the spelling it was written with. a type test may not join a chain at all —
# python's chaining rule would ask whether the *class* has the next type
e = xs === xs !== None

# mixed with value comparisons
f = 1 === 1 == 1

# parenthesised operands
g = (xs) === (xs)
h = (xs) !== (xs)

# a comment between the operands, and a line continuation — the two the old
# source-gap scan read wrong
i = (
    xs
    # which one is this
    === xs
)
j = xs \
    === xs

# inside a condition
if xs === xs:
    pass

# a long chain that has to break
long_chain = (
    some_rather_long_name === another_rather_long_name
    and another_rather_long_name !== yet_another_long_name
)
```

## Output
```bython
# basedpython spells identity as `===` / `!==`. both parse to the `CmpOp` of
# `is` / `is not`, whose surface form is instead a parametric type test, so the
# two spellings must not be collapsed into one

xs = [1]

a = xs === xs
b = xs !== xs

# the `is` spelling is a type test and stays as written
c = xs is list[int]
d = xs is not list[int]

# a chain of identity comparisons is ordinary python, and each operator keeps
# the spelling it was written with. a type test may not join a chain at all —
# python's chaining rule would ask whether the *class* has the next type
e = xs === xs !== None

# mixed with value comparisons
f = 1 === 1 == 1

# parenthesised operands
g = (xs) === (xs)
h = (xs) !== (xs)

# a comment between the operands, and a line continuation — the two the old
# source-gap scan read wrong
i = (
    xs
    # which one is this
    === xs
)
j = xs === xs

# inside a condition
if xs === xs:
    pass

# a long chain that has to break
long_chain = (
    some_rather_long_name === another_rather_long_name
    and another_rather_long_name !== yet_another_long_name
)
```
